@startuml
!include _style.iuml
' Speaker note: Problem: isolate private-media I/O and AWS command types from compilation/capture consumers.
' Speaker note: Candidates: repeat backend branches in jobs, or inject a MediaStore strategy with an S3 transport adapter.
' Speaker note: Choice: MediaStore + PrivateS3Transport; the privateTransport(sdk) returned object maps SDK commands. Local disk mode remains config.media=null.
title Design class view · Media storage
skinparam nodesep 25
skinparam ranksep 30
class "stored-output.ts" as CTX <<context>> {
  + storedContext(options, groupId)
}
interface MediaStore <<strategy>> #EEE7F3 {
  + put(scope, input)
  + head(scope, ref)
  + read(scope, ref)
  + delete(scope, ref)
}
class LocalMediaStore <<concrete strategy>> #F5F2E9
class PrivateS3MediaStore <<concrete strategy>> #F5F2E9 {
  - transport: PrivateS3Transport
}
interface PrivateS3Transport <<target>> #EEE7F3 {
  + putObject(input)
  + headObject(input)
  + getObject(input)
  + deleteObject(input)
}
class "runtime-store.ts\nprivateTransport(sdk)" as AD <<adapter>> #F5F2E9
class "AWS SDK v3\nS3Client + *Command" as SDK <<adaptee>> #FCF7E7
CTX -right-> MediaStore : uses 0..1
LocalMediaStore .up.|> MediaStore
PrivateS3MediaStore .up.|> MediaStore
' Realization is interface implementation for both stores.
LocalMediaStore -[hidden]right- PrivateS3MediaStore
PrivateS3MediaStore -right-> PrivateS3Transport
AD .up.|> PrivateS3Transport : returns object
AD -right-> SDK : send(command)
legend bottom
  createMediaRuntime(config) selects LocalMediaStore or PrivateS3MediaStore.
  Hosted dev uses S3. Local disk mode sets config.media = null.
endlegend
@enduml
